BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Forro Roots Weekend Toronto - Brazilian Dance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T210000
UID:blogto-237246@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/30/original_imagead25d1b0-7459-4560-8058-2bca9d6255
 ca.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto dance community is set to host the city's inaugura
 l Forró Roots Weekend on July 11–12\, 2026\, marking the exclusive firs
 t stop of a multi-city Canadian tour that will continue on to Montreal and
  Quebec City.\nHeld at the newly opened Tempo Dance Collective (1610A Bloo
 r St W)\, the intensive weekend brings world-class international instructi
 on directly to Ontario. The event features specialized workshops led by gu
 est instructor Julie Médous from the acclaimed São Paulo-based project\,
  Viajando Pelo Roots.\nForró Roots represents a contemporary\, sensitive\
 , and deeply interactive approach to partner dance. Characterized by intri
 cate legwork\, a strong emphasis on musicality\, and a nuanced physical co
 nnection\, the style is grounded in traditional Forró pé de serra while 
 seamlessly weaving in structural elements drawn from Forró de Itaúnas\, 
 Samba de Gafieira\, and Tango. It functions as a living language\, constan
 tly transforming within global social dance communities.\nThe Toronto edit
 ion of this international workshop series is organized by local journalist
  and cultural producer Raquel Camargo.\nWhat: Forró Roots Weekend (Worksh
 ops & Socials)\nWhen: July 11–12\, 2026\nWhere: Tempo Dance Collective\,
  1610A Bloor St W\, Toronto
LOCATION:Tempo Dance Collective
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/forro-roots-weekend-toronto-brazilian-da
 nce-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
