 gto.com/events/2026/06/23/original_image08016789-c5e4-44e5-9256-c1ac11b7a4
 05.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A stand up host is the most powerful person in the room\, and 
 most comics have no idea how to do it well.\nGreat hosts can save a bad sh
 ow\, elevate a good show\, and make a great show unforgettable.\nThis 4 ho
 ur in-class workshop is deisnged to teach the essential skills of hosting 
 a stand-up comedy show\; from opening a show with confidence to introducin
 g comedians properly\, managing the room\, the do's and don'ts of hosting\
 , and handling real-time challenges like hecklers or low energy crowds.\nT
 aught by one of the most sought after hosts in the country\, John Mostyn\,
  a professional stand up comedian with over ten years of experience\, this
  course focuses on practical\, real-life hosting skills you can apply imme
 diately.\nHosting for Stand-Up 101 is ideal for comics with some stage exp
 erience who watn to become a more versatile performer and become a more va
 luable and bookable comedian.
LOCATION:Comedy Bar East
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/hosting-for-stand-up-101-with-john-mosty
 n-toronto/
