DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T133000
UID:blogto-237481@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/07/06/original_image2b0da2df-a6b8-443f-9cfc-ffe7352d68
 3b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Step into a realm of deep presence and rejuvenation with the S
 low Sundays Hammock Sound Bath experience. Set in a serene sensory environ
 ment\, you will be gently cradled in a supportive\, cozy cotton hammock. T
 he session will begin with a somatic progressive relaxation exercise\, fol
 lowed by a journey through sound\, featuring a variety of live instruments
  such as singing bowls\, drums\, a gong and shakers. Their vibrations have
  the power to resonate through the body\, releasing tension and promoting 
 deep healing. After the sound bath\, you'll have a few moments to gently a
 waken with grounding frequencies and optional aromas. This unique experien
 ce can harmonize the body\, mind and spirit\, offering the potential for a
  profound sense of peace and tranquility.\nI am the guide\, you are your h
 ealer. When you are relieved of the stress and responsibilities of your da
 y-to-day life\, even for a short while\, your body's natural healing abili
 ties have the space to be activated.\nPOTENTIAL BENEFITS OF A HAMMOCK SOUN
 D BATH\n• Deep Relaxation: The gentle rocking of the hammock combined wi
 th intentional sound frequencies can lull your body into a deeply relaxed 
 state\, helping to relieve stress and anxiety.\n• Enhanced Circulation: 
 Being suspended in the air allows for optimal blood flow and circulation\,
  promoting physical well-being.\n• Pain Alleviation: The weightlessness 
 of the hammock may reduce pressure on the joints and muscles\, providing r
 elief from chronic pain or tension.\n• Emotional Liberation: The sound v
 ibrations may help release emotional blockages\, fostering a sense of emot
 ional balance and clarity.\n• Sleep Reimagined: Many participants report
  improved sleep patterns after a hammock sound bath\, as the experience he
 lps reset the nervous system and promotes a state of calm.\n• Spiritual 
 Connection: The combination of sound healing and gentle swaying can facili
 tate a deeper connection with your inner self\, enhancing your spiritual p
 ractice.
LOCATION:Jungle Flower Wellness
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/slow-sundays-hammock-sound-bath-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Steal this Story\, Please!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T204600
UID:blogto-236615@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/16/original_image13455199-1bee-46da-91f2-a39c5c1f3d
 9f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:#2 Top Audience Favourite\, Hot Docs Festival 2026\n“Gives u
 s insight into a truly inspirational woman. A career reporter who continue
 s to lean into the hard stories when a lot of media is pulling away. May t
 his film help us all to hold media accountable\, for its importance in sha
 ping the world should not be taken for granted.” – In The Seats\nWith 
 so much misinformation and bias in media reporting\, one thing that is fun
 damental to maintain is independent journalism. That’s where people like
  Amy Goodman and her independent news program Democracy Now! come into pla
 y. For decades\, Goodman has worked tirelessly to report unfiltered\, hard
 -hitting stories\, pressing upon those in power and trying to get to the b
 ottom of some of the most newsworthy stories. Relentless\, brave and ambit
 ious\, Goodman uses her platform to sidestep corporate media interference 
 and discuss topics that polarize people around the world. No subject is of
 f limits in her pursuit of truth. Academy Award nominees Carl Deal and Tia
  Lessin bring forth an intimate behind-the-scenes look at someone who upho
 lds the highest media standards while eschewing the bias that results from
  paid-for news time\, and has made a career of trying to amplify accuracy 
 and accountability. Gabor Pertic\, Hot Docs
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/steal-this-story-please-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
