BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lassonde Art Trail 'Wellbeing Walks' Series - Simon Pope: Sounding
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T190000
UID:blogto-237253@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/30/original_image6d900dc6-3757-4b53-aebf-6afc954d99
 9b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join the Lassonde Art Trail (LAT) for the first artist-led edi
 tion of its 'Wellbeing Walks' series\, where participants reflect on the i
 nterconnectedness between the wellbeing of self with the natural world.\
 nSoundings by Simon Pope with Austin Larusson and Tyler Prince invites wa
 lkers to consider their relationship to Lake Ontario and its watershed. A 
 group of walkers will be led along the pathways of Biidaasige Park by a si
 nger performing “sounding calls”\, as a way of attending to the fluct
 uations of both the water-level in Lake Ontario\, and our own fortunes in
  relation to it. Participants will encounter several LAT sculptures during
  the walk that will guide their experience.\nSimon Pope is an internationa
 lly renowned artist and researcher from the United Kingdom\, currently bas
 ed in Toronto\, Canada. \nAustin Larusson's recent appearances include so
 los in the Messiah with the Arcady ensemble. Upcoming engagements include 
 Jack in Earnest\, the Importance of Being with SOLT.\nTyler Prince is a
  baritone and saxophonist who is a graduate of the Phil & Eli Taylor Aca
 demy of the Royal Conservatory of Music.
LOCATION:Lassonde Art Trail
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/lassonde-art-trail-wellbeing-walks-serie
 s-simon-pope-soundings-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Le reve americain - Presented by the ICFF Festival at the Distille
 ry District
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T230000
UID:blogto-236894@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/23/original_image66de049d-839b-4c9f-bc6b-dddb4f081f
 37.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The agents who changed the game.\nJoin ICFF for a special scre
 ening of The American Dream\, a compelling story that explores ambition\, 
 identity\, and the shifting meaning of success in today’s world.\nSet ag
 ainst the backdrop of modern life and the pursuit of opportunity\, the fil
 m follows characters whose hopes and choices are shaped by the promise and
  pressure of “the American Dream.” As their lives intertwine\, long-he
 ld beliefs about success\, belonging\, and sacrifice are challenged\, reve
 aling how fragile and complex that dream can be.\nThe American Dream invit
 es audiences to reflect on what it truly means to build a life\, and at wh
 at cost. The film moves between moments of aspiration and reality\, captur
 ing the emotional tension between where we come from and where we hope to 
 go.\nDon’t miss this thought-provoking cinematic experience that examine
 s identity\, resilience\, and the pursuit of a better future\, asking a ti
 meless question: is the dream still the same for everyone who chases it?
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/le-reve-americain-presented-by-the-icff-
 festival-at-the-distillery-district-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
