 truction to elevate your figure drawing skills?\nOverview:\nIn this two-ho
 ur session seasoned animator and figure drawing teacher\, Sam Braithwaite\
 , will lead you in pushing the pose\, with a clear breakdown of what the t
 erm means and how to apply intent and life into your drawings while you wo
 rk from a live\, costumed model.\nWhether you are a new to exploring figur
 e drawing\, or have taken a break from drawing-from-life and are looking t
 o refresh your techniques\, this is a great way to ease yourself into the 
 practice and receive feedback in a supportive environment.\nPlease bring t
 he drawing materials you are comfortable with\, such as sketchbook\, newsp
 rint\, pencil\, conte and marker. Drawing boards will be available for use
 \, and additional materials will be available for purchase.\n\nAbout Your 
 Instructor:\nSam Braithwaite has been teaching figure drawing at Seneca Po
 lytechnic for 5 years and working in the animation industry for 13. Sam ha
 s worked on TV shows such as Blues Clues and You\, Wild Kratts\, and Angry
  Birds Summer Madness. For independents projects Sam has created music vid
 eos for Ria Mae and D.W Waterson and also showing paintings and drawings i
 n Toronto art galleries such as\, Atelier Next Door and Portrait Society o
 f Canada.\nTLDR\n✴︎ Professional figure drawing guidance\n✴︎ Live 
 costumed model\n✴︎ In-store discount for attendees + after hours retai
 l
