 be.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join Toronto author and Dinner With Strangers creator Jess Jan
 z for an interactive evening celebrating the launch of her debut book\, 'T
 he Table Where We Meet.'\nMore than a traditional author talk\, this homet
 own launch is designed to bring people together through meaningful convers
 ation\, storytelling\, and creative participation. Hosted by Jam Gamble\, 
 the evening will feature guided small-group discussions\, interactive conv
 ersation corners\, audience Q&A\, creative activations\, and a live conver
 sation exploring belonging\, friendship\, identity\, and what nearly a dec
 ade of gathering strangers has taught Jess about being human.\nWhether you
  arrive with friends or come on your own\, you'll leave having shared the 
 room (and likely a few stories!) with thoughtful people from across the ci
 ty.\nDate: Tuesday\, July 14\, 2026\nTime: 6:00 PM – 9:00 PM (doors at [
 insert time])\nLocation: The Great Hall\, 1087 Queen St W\, Toronto\nEveni
 ng Schedule\n6:00 PM: Doors open\, cash bar\, conversation corners & inter
 active activations\n6:30 PM: Welcome & guided small-group conversations\n7
 :00 PM: Jess Janz in conversation with Jam Gamble\n7:45 PM: Audience Q&A\n
 8:00 PM: Book signing\, mingling & interactive experiences\n9:00 PM: Event
  concludes (or "9:30 PM" if guests are welcome to linger)\nTickets\nTicket
 s are available on a tiered\, pay-what-feels-right model:\nCommunity Ticke
 t: $25\nGather Ticket: $35\nSet the Table Ticket: $50\nAll ticket tiers in
 clude the same experience. Guests who haven't already purchased the book m
 ay also bundle a copy of The Table Where We Meet with their ticket. Books 
 will be available on-site through Type Books\, and Jess will be signing co
 pies following the event.\nFor tickets and more information\, visit: jessj
 anz.com/book-tour
LOCATION:The Great Hall
