BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bronte: The World Without
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T211500
UID:blogto-236575@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/15/original_imagecd7ac6f4-bc6e-48a2-b967-b383b791c3
 7b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Brontë: The World Without is a glimpse into the lives of the 
 three famous sisters\, ​presenting an intimate look at their relationshi
 ps\, their artistic struggles\, the pressure of family responsibilities\, 
 and the sisterhood that helped them achieve greatness.\nPresented outdoors
  at the iconic Greek Theatre in Guild Park & Gardens\, this play illuminat
 es how the Brontë’s experiences echo those of the heroines who live on 
 in their beloved and unforgettable novels such as Jane Eyre and Wuthering 
 Heights.\nA must-see for Brontë fans\, Brontë: The World Without is an u
 nflinching portrayal of family\, artistry\, and what it means to strive fo
 r success in a world that often denies women the right to dream.\nGuild Fe
 stival Theatre’s 2026 Season is presented by ARC Insurance & Financial S
 ervices Inc.\nWritten by Jordi Mand\nDirected by Helen Juvonen\nCostume De
 sign by Alex Amini\nSound Design by Maddie Bautista\nLighting Design by Ho
 ney Hoseiny\nProduction Design by Elisia Evans\nFeaturing Laura Del Papa\,
  Hilary Scott & Lara Lucia
LOCATION:Guild Festival Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/bronte-the-world-without-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
