BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Big Stories in Little India
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T163000
UID:blogto-236713@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/18/original_image9d5e934e-4d5b-4c62-a5ff-470c38f6ad
 d2.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Discover how a former industrial brickyard is now a hub for To
 ronto’s South Asian community.\nLearn how one of Toronto’s first Bolly
 wood movie theatres transformed this East End neighbourhood into an intern
 ational destination for South Asian culture during the 1970s and 1980s.\nO
 n this walk\, we’ll explore this unparalled bazaar\, a business-based en
 clave formed by multiple entrepreneurial immigrants\, stopping at location
 s like the Lahore Tikka House\, known for barbecued green chilies\, and Ch
 andan Fashion\, the star of the reality show Bollywed.\nThis emerging hist
 orian tour will be developed and led by Sarah Takhar\, an international re
 searcher and museum educator who has worked with organisations such as the
  Museum on the Mound\, the Scottish Maritime Museum\, the Aurora Historica
 l Society\, and currently the Museum of Dufferin. Sarah is passionate abou
 t investigating heritage through a transnational lens\, and exploring the 
 cross-cultural connections of history.\nThis tour is provided for $8.00/pe
 rson. The total cost is $10.05 (includes a $2.05 transaction fee). Please 
 note that space is limited on our tours. You may not be able to join a tou
 r group if you have not registered ahead of time through our website. Cash
  cannot be accepted onsite.
LOCATION:Start Point - Greenwood Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/big-stories-in-little-india-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
