 gto.com/events/2026/07/05/original_image7feeb025-7faa-43ad-90be-ef78369d3d
 04.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Destiny Events is turning 33 this year\, and we are celebratin
 g the way we know best. On July 18th\, 2026\, we are bringing Dillinja to 
 CODA in Toronto. One of the most important producers and DJs drum & bass h
 as ever produced\, Dillinja has been shaping the sound and feel of this mu
 sic since 1991. His basslines hit harder than almost anything you will eve
 r hear on a dancefloor\, and his sets carry the kind of weight that only c
 omes from three decades of total dedication to the culture. This is a rare
  Toronto appearance from a true legend of the genre.
LOCATION:Coda
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/dillinja-a-drumbass-legend-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edible & Medicinal Plants of Ontario with Stephan Lukacic in Toron
 to's High Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T160000
UID:blogto-237024@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/25/original_imagecca95b6e-9ed2-4c09-8c58-ea858e8162
 c9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Take an introductory peek into nature’s pantry and pharmacy 
 with popular outdoor educator and avid forager Stephan Lukacic.\nThis fasc
 inating workshop is focused on plant anatomy and identification skills\, a
 nd the sustainable harvest of common wild plants for food and medicine.\nE
 xploring wild plant ecology\, traditional uses\, and the modern science be
 hind it all\, this comprehensive class will not only teach you how to iden
 tify wild plants safely and accurately\, but Steve will share some of his 
 favorite ways of using them\, including delicious recipes and tried-and-tr
 ue home remedies.\nThe list of plants covered in this workshop includes na
 tive\, naturalized\, and invasive species that have both culinary and heal
 ing properties\, many of which can be found right in your own backyard. Yo
 u will receive an 8-page handout covering all the basics of plant identifi
 cation and ethical foraging\, and read and discuss its contents thoroughly
 . Then you’ll do a deep dive right onto the trails in High Park — putt
 ing the knowledge you’ve acquired directly into practice by observing an
 d identifying wild plants the group encounters in their natural habitat.\n
 Come learn everything you ever wanted to know about wild plants and a whol
 e lot more… There’s always time for questions and conversation\, cool 
 people and a bunch of laughs!\nNote: You will not be foraging for wild pla
 nts to take home. This workshop focuses on teaching you how to find and id
 entify wild edible and medicinal plants.\nPrice: $73\nAges: 18+ years\nMee
 ting Location: High Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodge Drive\nPlease 
 bring:\nA pen or pencil\nA notebook\nWeather-appropriate clothing\nCuriosi
 ty\nReadiness for outdoor learning
LOCATION:High Park Nature Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/edible-medicinal-plants-of-ontario-with-
 stephan-lukacic-in-torontos-high-park-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Frequency: Shel Khan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T220000
UID:blogto-237397@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/07/03/original_image6de583b3-ef84-4a5d-9d62-4d540a280f
 5c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Jul 18\n8pm\n$15-$20 adv\n$25 doors\nJoin us for Frequency —
  a monthly live music series at Worth Gallery.\nFrequency spotlights BIPOC
  musicians of varying genres through intimate\, stripped-back shows. Celeb
 rating sound\, connection\, and creative expression in Toronto's vibrant m
 usic scene. Find your new favorite musician in your new favorite gallery.\
 nThis month's edition of Frequency features Shel Khan\, an existential gen
 re bending musician exploring different aspects of human life in her sound
 .\nShel Khan is a Toronto-based musician blending alternative\, grunge\, s
 oul\, and industrial music. Her sound is fierce\, vulnerable\, and evocati
 ve\, with songs exploring themes of ancestry\, nature\, consciousness\, lo
 ss\, human connection\, existentialism\, Buddhism\, and dialectics.\nHuman
  life contains soaring highs\, bleak lows\, beauty\, violence\, and everyt
 hing in between. Shel aspires to touch as much of that multitude as possib
 le.\nHer debut self-produced EP\, Garden\, released May 8\, 2026\, marks a
  shift toward a darker\, soulful\, post-industrial alt-rock sound and is o
 nly the beginning.
LOCATION:Worth Gallery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/frequency-shel-khan-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
