DESCRIPTION:Celebrate World Snake Day by spending the morning with High Pa
 rk Nature Centre learning about the different snakes who call Ontario home
 . From Massasauga Rattlers in Bruce County to High Park’s very own Garte
 r Snakes\, there are twelve species across the province with unique lifecy
 cles\, habitat requirements\, and conservation challenges. Often misunders
 tood\, snakes are fascinating animals. Get to know them better on this fam
 ily-friendly nature walk in Toronto’s High Park.\nPrice: $10\nAges: Fami
 ly Friendly\nMeeting Location: High Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodg
 e Drive
