BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:African Artistry: A September Collective Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T180000
UID:blogto-237270@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/30/original_image7e290816-c6e9-4341-8646-4c22327c8f
 49.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, September Collective opens a curated space in th
 e heart of Dundas West where you can discover handcrafted modern objects f
 rom African and diaspora artisans\, participate in cultural activations\, 
 and connect with a community that believes your home should tell a story.\
 nFor four days (July 23-26)\, explore heritage-inspired modern African hom
 e decor and art. From hand-blown recycled glass vases crafted in Nairobi t
 o sustainably sourced wooden sculptures from Accra (created from reclaimed
  plantation waste through a partnership with Ghana's Forestry Commission) 
 and hand-woven basketry from Bolgatanga. Every piece is attributed to its 
 maker\, celebrating the artistry\, heritage\, and craftsmanship behind eac
 h object.\nParticipate in activations designed to be felt\, not just seen:
  blend and pour your own candle in a hand-blown Moroccan glass vessel with
  Villa Aburi (July 24\, 6:00-7:30 PM\, $125\, limited to 10 spots). A flor
 al design experience is also planned for Sunday with details coming soon. 
 The residency sits steps from OssFest\, acclaimed restaurants like Patois 
 and The Lunch Lady\, Trinity Bellwoods Park\, and Ode Hotel\, Toronto's on
 ly Black-owned boutique hotel. Come for the objects. Stay for the communit
 y.\nEvent Details:\nDates: July 23-26\, 2026\nHours: 9:00 AM - 6:00 PM dai
 ly\nAdmission: Free (general walk-through)\nWorkshops: Candle Making Exp\,
  July 24\, 6:00-7:30 PM\, $125 per person (10 spots available)\, Floral De
 sign Experience - Details to come
LOCATION:Dundas West Studio
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/african-artistry-a-september-collective-
 experience-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
