 or Allison Glenn in conversation in Baillie Court to mark the opening of t
 he new exhibition\, Dawoud Bey: Material Histories\, Living Landscapes. AG
 O Curator Julie Crooks will moderate.\nFeaturing a film and 23 photographs
 \, in dialogue with four African sculptures from the AGO Collection\, Bey 
