BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Muneeb Hermans Septet feat. Lorraine Klaasen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T230000
UID:blogto-237330@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/07/02/original_image70559ca7-fd9a-41c7-a216-223ae7c771
 55.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Acclaimed Cape Town–born trumpeter Muneeb Hermans brings his
  expanded septet to the Redwood Theatre for a special performance featurin
 g Juno Award-winning vocalist Lorraine Klaasen.\nKnown for his soulful sou
 nd\, expressive compositions\, and collaborations across South Africa and 
 beyond\, Hermans has performed internationally from Carnegie Hall to major
  jazz festivals throughout Europe\, Africa\, and North America. For this c
 oncert\, he joins forces with Klaasen\, one of Canada's leading world musi
 c artists\, for an evening of South African jazz\, original music\, and ex
 ceptional ensemble playing.\nThroughout the month of July\, audiences can 
 also catch Muneeb Hermans in a series of performances with different ensem
 bles at CONTXT by Trane\, culminating with this special expanded septet co
 ncert at the Redwood Theatre.\nPerformance Details:\nSaturday\, July 25\, 
 2026\nMuneeb Hermans Septet featuring Lorraine Klaasen\nRedwood Theatre\nD
 oors: 7:00 PM | Show: 8:00–11:00 PM\nTickets: $40 advance | $50 at the d
 oor\nLineup:\nMuneeb Hermans – Trumpet\nLorraine Klaasen – Vocals\nRob
  Christian – Saxophone\nKwando Harris – Keyboard\nDally Dominic – Ba
 ss\nMario Leed Posella – Guitar\nKoffie – Drums\nAbout Muneeb Hermans\
 nBorn in Cape Town\, South Africa\, Muneeb Hermans began his musical journ
 ey in the vibrant Cape Minstrel tradition before studying Jazz Performance
  at the University of Cape Town. Today\, he is recognized as one of South 
 Africa's leading trumpet players\, with performances spanning the UK\, Fra
 nce\, Spain\, China\, the Seychelles\, and the United States\, including a
 n appearance at Carnegie Hall.\nA regular at South Africa's premier jazz f
 estivals\, including the Cape Town International Jazz Festival\, Standard 
 Bank Joy of Jazz\, and the National Youth Jazz Festival\, Hermans has shar
 ed the stage with renowned artists such as Caiphus Semenya\, Jimmy Dludlu\
 , Errol Dyers\, Buddy Wells\, Benjamin Jephta\, and Marcus Wyatt. His accl
 aimed debut album\, *One for HP*\, showcases his distinctive compositional
  voice and is available on all major streaming platforms.\nAbout Lorraine 
 Klaasen\nJuno Award-winning vocalist Lorraine Klaasen is one of Canada's f
 oremost ambassadors of African music. Based in London\, Ontario\, she is t
 he daughter of legendary South African jazz singer Thandi Klaasen and has 
 captivated audiences around the world with her vibrant stage presence and 
 powerful voice.\nHer international career has taken her to major festivals
  throughout North America\, Mexico\, and the Caribbean\, including the Mon
 treal International Jazz Festival. In 2013\, she received the Juno Award f
 or World Music Album of the Year for *A Tribute to Miriam Makeba*. Togethe
 r with her mother\, she was also regarded as one of Nelson Mandela's favor
 ite performers.
LOCATION:Redwood Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/muneeb-hermans-septet-feat-lorraine-klaa
 sen-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
