BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crowd Work with Dylan Gott
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260726T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260726T150000
UID:blogto-237186@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/29/original_image9edbd767-4f5f-48d5-a919-44b994d981
 00.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Unlock the Secret to Seamless Crowd Command: Join “Crowd Wor
 k with Dylan Gott” – A Hands-On Workshop\nAre you ready to transform e
 very audience member into your partner in comedy? Whether you’re a buddi
 ng stand-up looking to break the ice or a seasoned comedian aiming to shar
 pen your improv instincts\, Crowd work with Dylan Gott\, will equip you wi
 th the tools\, confidence\, and live-stage practice you need to conquer an
 y room.\nWhy Crowd Work Matters\nElevate Your Act: Spontaneous interaction
  keeps your set fresh and unpredictable.\nRecover Gracefully: Learn to han
 dle hecklers\, awkward silences\, and unexpected curveballs with poise.\nC
 rowd Control: Feel comfortable in any situation - bar show\, comedy club\,
  corporate or just if your jokes aren't working that night\nWhat You’ll 
 Walk Away With\nFoundations of Engagement\nTechniques for reading energy a
 nd identifying “ripe” audience members.\nOpeners and ice-breakers that
  spark genuine responses.\nStructuring Your Spontaneity\nChange your respo
 nses based on your role on the show\nHow to weave crowd responses into you
 r existing material.\nAdvanced Tactics\nHandling hecklers vs when to go fo
 r the throat\nHow to handle unruly audience members based on your role on 
 the show\nWho Should Attend\nOpen-mic hopefuls hungry to break into paid g
 igs\nPro-am comedians aiming to level up their engagement\nPublic Speakers
  prepare for your next presentation by being able to improv easily off the
  cuff
LOCATION:Comedy Bar East
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/crowd-work-with-dylan-gott-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
