BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reclaim Your Voice: Song Circle & Sound Bath for Women who have ex
 perienced Abuse & S.A.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T203000
UID:blogto-237134@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/27/original_imagee2d65e38-357f-46d8-ad1c-982a649ab9
 3c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join song-carrier and certified music therapist Michaela for a
  community song circle to nourish the heart. At the beginning of every lin
 eage there was a fire\, a drum\, and a song. Elder and community song-lead
 er Laurence Cole reminds that “song is one of our most ancient technolog
 ies of belonging.” We gather to remember our innate connection to sound\
 , breath\, and rhythm. To play\, laugh\, cry\, and bow in reverence to our
  collective aliveness. This is a space to bring your joy\, your grief\, an
 d everything in between. We will explore simple songs and juicy layered ha
 rmonies through the oral tradition of call and response. No prior experien
 ce with singing is necessary. Whether you are passionate for solo singing\
 , campfire jams\, or someone who believes “I am not a singer\,” this s
 pace is for you.\nThe gathering will close with a soothing sound bath to s
 upport integration and release. A sound bath is a full-body listening expe
 rience\, featuring live frequencies including crystal singing bowls\, voic
 e\, drum\, and more. These vibrations have been shown to activate therapeu
 tic processes such as regulating the nervous system\, softening physical t
 ension\, slowing the brainwaves\, and cultivating deep cellular rest.\nThi
 s session is planned to take place outdoors\, just prior to sunset. Please
  wear what makes you feel most comfortable\, considering cozy layers and a
 dditional props like blanket/mat\, journal\, water bottle\, insect repelle
 nt\, and a small pillow or folding chair for seating.\nOptional: bring one
  small item that connects you to the earth (stone\, feather\, flower\, fru
 it) as we build a collective centrepiece of beauty to anchor us.
LOCATION:Corktown Common Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/reclaim-your-voice-song-circle-sound-bat
 h-for-women-who-have-experienced-abuse-sa-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
