BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Convergence of Coasts in Tkaronto\; Where The Trees Meet is an e
 xperimental jazz showcase.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T233000
UID:blogto-237370@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/07/03/original_image94e310bb-3aad-420f-b23b-bf53c3a65b
 74.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A night of sound and connection\, celebrating the meeting of c
 oasts on Tkaronto\nA Convergence of Coasts in Tkaronto\; Where The Trees M
 eet is an experimental jazz showcase. Join us for a night of sound and con
 nection\, celebrating the meeting of coasts on Tkaronto. TICKETS: $10 at h
 ttps://www.eventbrite.ca/e/a-convergence-of-coasts-in-tkaronto-where-the-t
 rees-meet-tickets-1992773112022\nFrom the salt of the Atlantic to the puls
 e of the Pacific to the shores of the Great Lakes\, three artists\, three 
 territories\, one city.\nFeaturing\nSKYLA J & OZ (Vancouver / Salish Terri
 tory) | LISTEN HERE: https://www.youtube.com/@SkylaJ\nSkyla J and Oz - Aft
 er nearly a decade-long hiatus since Greenlaw\, UK recording artists Skyla
  J and Oz return with a bold and deeply personal new chapter. The couple u
 nveils a fresh sonic landscape that fuses soulful songwriting\, lush elect
 ronic production\, deep dub rhythms\, jazz-infused textures\, and the atmo
 spheric pulse of trip hop Drawing on decades of musical collaboration whil
 e embracing new creative territory\, Skyla J and Oz deliver a sound that f
 eels both timeless and forward-looking. More than a comeback\, this is an 
 evolution\, a powerful re-emergence from artists whose passion\, chemistry
 \, and creative vision continue to resonate with depth\, authenticity\, an
 d soul.\nLAL (Toronto / Tkaronto) | LISTEN HERE: https://www.youtube.com/@
 lalforestworld\nFor over two decades\, Polaris Prize–longlisted Toronto 
 duo LAL\; Bengali-rooted vocalist and activist Rosina Kazi and Barbados-bo
 rn producer Nicholas “Murr” Murray\, have built a catalogue of silvery
 \, internationally influenced electronica that insists the dancefloor rema
 in a site of resistance and renewal. The first single from LAL’s new LP\
 , titled "Practice Of Love" is "Shadows Of Your Dreams"\, which released i
 n March 2026. This offering shares an emotional and philosophical tone for
  a body of work forged through personal and collective transformation. Thi
 s new LP was created in deep collaboration with a chosen family\, includin
 g multidisciplinary artists\, Victor Robert Kee III aka Folke\, Ange Loft\
 , musicians V and Ian de Souza\, filmmakers Jose Garcia and Jaek Eastcott\
 , and Jaws\, whose care and coordination hold the work together. This coll
 aborative process is not incidental—it reflects the album’s central in
 sistence that art\, like survival\, is something we do together.\nDILSHAN 
 (Halifax/ Kjipuktuk) | LISTEN HERE: https://dilshan.bandcamp.com/album/re-
 fuge\nBorn and raised in Halifax\, NS\, Dilshan is an artist\, musician\, 
 and music scholar. He performed with artists such as Michael Kaeshammer\, 
 Regina Carter\, multi-JUNO winner Hilario Duran\, and GRAMMY nominee Ignac
 io Berroa. He has studied and performed with artists from numerous differe
 nt backgrounds\, from jazz guitarist Lorne Lofsky\, to composer and Chance
  the Rapper collaborator JoVia Armstrong\, to Guggenheim award winners suc
 h as poet Brian Teare and composer and flutist Nicole Mitchell. He release
 d his debut record "re:fuge" in September 2025- a live album exploring Afr
 odiasporic musical language as a means of building a space of refuge throu
 gh music. Dilshan's music draws from a host of styles\, from indie R&B to 
 soul jazz\, to Hip-hop influenced Neo-soul\, and Afro-Surrealist free impr
 ovisation\, with a unique sound that will delight fans of Sampha and Frank
  Ocean\, indie fans of Dijon and Bon Iver\, and Hip-hop jazz fans of Rober
 t Glasper\, Tom Misch\, and Yussef Dayes. Currently\, he is doing a PhD in
  Music\, working with Hip-hop artist\, educator\, and scholar\, A.D Carson
 .\nPresented by Pineapple Express Media Inc.
LOCATION:Tranzac Club
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/a-convergence-of-coasts-in-tkaronto-wher
 e-the-trees-meet-is-an-experimental-jazz-showcase-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
