BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:PalmHouse Sessions Present : The Music of J Dilla
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T230000
UID:blogto-236826@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/22/original_image40cf0b19-6afe-4b8b-a2c9-b56b73ddc3
 6a.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Rediscover J Dilla's iconic catalog through live band renditio
 ns of both his rarest and most famous tracks. Live from Allan Gardens Palm
 house\nEarly Bird tickets on sale now!\nThere are places in Toronto that h
 old memory.\nThe historic Palm House at Allan Gardens is one of them.\nFor
  generations\, Allan Gardens has been a place of refuge\, beauty\, gatheri
 ng\, and quiet wonder in the heart of downtown Toronto. Its glass conserva
 tory has offered warmth in the winter\, shade in the summer\, and a rare s
 ense of calm in the middle of the city.\nNow\, this beloved public space i
 s entering a new chapter.\nPalmhouse Sessions is a new live music series c
 reated to bring the historic Palm House alive once again through community
 \, culture\, and local Toronto talent. Presented in partnership with Frien
 ds of Allan Gardens\, the series invites people back into the conservatory
  in a new way.Set against a lush backdrop of tropical plants and flowers\,
  with the Palm House’s glass dome overhead and the night sky above\, Pal
 mhouse Sessions offers a rare experience in the heart of the city: intimat
 e\, atmospheric\, and impossible to recreate anywhere else in Toronto.\nBr
 ing your friends\, take your photos\, capture the moment. The FOMO will be
  real!\nFor the first edition\, Palmhouse Sessions pays tribute to J Dilla
 \, one of the most influential producers in hip-hop history\, whose sound 
 continues to shape jazz\, soul\, R&B\, electronic music\, and beat culture
  across generations.\nThe Music\nThis one of a kind musical experience wil
 l bring listeners on a journey through the soundcapes and moods of J Dilla
 's catalog\, all performed live with a 4-piece band.\nNever before heard l
 ive arrangements and mashups of his beats and songs with breathe new life 
 into these iconic tracks\, and will showcase a blend of his most famous an
 d well known works\, as well as extremely rare "deep-cuts" that few have e
 ver heard.\nExpect to hear tracks he made for Slum Village\, The Pharcyde\
 , Common\, Erykah Badu\, D'Angelo\, The Roots\, and many others.\nEnjoy Vi
 nyl DJ sets of strictly J Dilla tunes during the band setbreaks.\nPerforme
 rs\nSB Tones on Sax\, Flute\, Vocoder\, Ewi\, Bandleader\nDarryl Joseph on
  Dennie - Keyboards\nSean Dennis on Bass\nJon Catanus on Drums\nOpening So
 unds by Vinyl DJ Gil Masuda\nCash Bar\nA cash bar will be available throug
 hout the evening featuring cocktails\, wine\, and beer.\nThe evening will 
 also feature a signature cocktail\, with proceeds supporting Friends of Al
 lan Gardens’ planned expansion of the Allan Gardens Conservatory. The ex
 pansion vision calls for growing the conservatory’s footprint and revita
 lizing the surrounding parkland to create more space for gardens\, public 
 programming\, education\, culture\, and community gathering.\nGuests are e
 ncouraged to learn more and sign the expansion petition here:\nExpand the 
 Conservatory at Allan Gardens:\nTransportation\nGuests are encouraged to w
 alk\, bike\, or take transit to Allan Gardens whenever possible.\nBy TTC: 
 The Conservatory is located near the Carlton streetcar route\, with access
  from nearby subway stations including College Station and Sherbourne stat
 ion.\nBy bike: Bike Share Toronto is available at the northeast corner of 
 Allan Gardens\, and bicycle parking is available throughout the park and s
 urrounding area.\nBy car: Parking in the area is limited. Street parking m
 ay be available on nearby streets\, and\nGreen P municipal paid parking is
  available nearby at 450 Sherbourne St.\nAbout Palmhouse Sessions\nPalmhou
 se Sessions is a new live music series presented in partnership with Frien
 ds of Allan Gardens\, created to bring music\, culture\, and community int
 o the heart of the historic Allan Gardens Conservatory.\nThe series celebr
 ates the Palm House as a beloved public landmark and part of Toronto’s c
 ultural history. Each session is designed as an intimate gathering that co
 nnects place\, sound\, community\, and local creativity.\nBy supporting Pa
 lmhouse Sessions\, guests are also supporting a broader vision for Allan G
 ardens: a more vibrant\, welcoming\, and animated public space where cultu
 re and community can thrive.\nAbout Friends of Allan Gardens\nFriends of A
 llan Gardens is the community stewardship organization dedicated to suppor
 ting the care\, animation\, and long-term future of Allan Gardens.\nThroug
 h public programming\, cultural partnerships\, community events\, advocacy
 \, and on-the-ground stewardship\, FOAG works to strengthen Allan Gardens 
 as a welcoming\, vibrant\, and well-loved public space for Toronto residen
 ts and visitors.\nAs a partner in Palmhouse Sessions\, FOAG is helping bri
 ng new cultural programming into the conservatory while supporting the bro
 ader revitalization and community life of Allan Gardens.\nFOAG is also lea
 ding public advocacy for the planned expansion of the Allan Gardens Conser
 vatory\, a once-in-a-generation civic project to grow the conservatory\, i
 mprove the surrounding parkland\, and strengthen Allan Gardens as a year-r
 ound destination for horticulture\, culture\, education\, and community li
 fe.\nAccessibility\, Washrooms & Notes\nEveryone is welcome. The Allan Gar
 dens Conservatory is fully accessible\, and accessible washrooms are avail
 able in the Orchid-Bromeliad House\, the southernmost house in the Conserv
 atory.\nThis is a limited-capacity event. Please arrive early to allow tim
 e for entry.\nDoors at 7pm. Music begins at 7:45pm
LOCATION:The Palmhouse at Allan Gardens
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/palmhouse-sessions-present-the-music-of-
 j-dilla-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
