BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jane Austen's Northanger Abbey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T210000
UID:blogto-236598@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/16/original_imaged8a69feb-decf-4514-a847-24a2a253e8
 be.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Northanger Abbey\, Jane Austen’s satire of the Gothic novel 
 craze\, is brought to life in a hilarious\, whirlwind production by the di
 rector of last year's hit The 39 Steps!\nCatherine Morland loves reading t
 he latest books but she lets her imagination run wild\, finding Gothic mys
 tery in the most mundane corners of England. As the clichés of the Horrid
  Novels spill into her reality\, Catherine's simple holiday is transformed
  into a personal adventure filled with mischief and romance.\nPresented ou
 tdoors at the iconic Greek Theatre in Guild Park & Gardens\, this new adap
 tation of Austen's charming coming-of-age story is a funny and fast-paced 
 journey of first love and self-discovery.\nGuild Festival Theatre’s 2026
  Season is presented by ARC Insurance & Financial Services Inc.\nAdapted &
  Directed by Tyler J. Seguin\nCostume Design by Alex Amini\nProduction Des
 ign by Elisia Evans\nLighting Design by Honey Hoseiny\nSound Design by Sha
 wn Piccione\nStage Manager Kiera Doerksen Smith\nChoreographer & Assistant
  Stage Manager Leah Wilton\nAssistant Director Bonnie Duff\nFeaturing\nGeo
 rgia Findlay\nIsaiah Kolundzic\nAndrew Prashad\nKiana Woo\nAugust 6th-23rd
 \, $16.25-$32.50
LOCATION:Guild Festival Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/jane-austens-northanger-abbey-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
