 52.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Etobicoke’s waterfront is set to come alive once again as th
 e Humber Bay Shores Waterfront Festival returns for another year of live m
 usic\, food\, and lakeside fun along the shores of Lake Ontario.\nTaking p
 lace in Humber Bay Shores Park along Marine Parade Drive\, the free two-da
 y festival transforms the waterfront into a vibrant community hub featurin
 g local vendors\, food trucks\, artisan markets\, and family-friendly acti
 vities—all with sweeping skyline views in the background.\nVisitors can 
 expect a full lineup of entertainment throughout the weekend\, including l
 ive bands\, DJs\, plus a packed schedule of activities by the lake.\nThe f
 estival also highlights one of its biggest draws: a curated local vendor m
 arketplace\, featuring handmade goods\, small businesses\, food artisans\,
  and specialty products from across Etobicoke and the GTA. From baked good
 s and street food to crafts and lifestyle brands\, the market is designed 
 to showcase the best of the local community.\nFamilies are well covered to
 o\, with a dedicated Kids Zone featuring games\, face painting\, and inter
 active activities designed to keep younger festivalgoers busy all day.\nFo
 od is a major focus\, with a wide selection of local eateries and food tru
 cks serving everything from quick street eats to sweet treats—perfect fo
 r a lakeside picnic on the grass.\nOrganizers say the goal of the festival
  is to celebrate Humber Bay’s growing community while activating the wat
 erfront with accessible\, inclusive programming that brings together resid
 ents\, visitors\, and local businesses.\nThe Humber Bay Shores Waterfront 
