BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Theatre In St. James Park Presents 1920s Walking Around In A Dream
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T170000
UID:blogto-236718@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/18/original_imageff27a4fa-03d8-4a4c-9252-c95f0ac0cb
 9b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:No Ticket Required. BYO chair or blanket.\nRuntime: approx 1 h
 our.\nHoopty-doo! Grab your glad rags\, we’re putting on the Ritz!\nOld 
 Town Toronto BIA and Alumnae Theatre present Unspoken Theatre’s new\
 , family friendly musical comedy\, 1920’s Walking Around In A Dream.\nT
 he hour long live performance inspired by Shakespeare’s A Midsummer Nig
 ht’s Dream\, brings the Roaring Twenties jazz age alive for the 2020’s
 ! The show has jazz classics by Cole Porter\, “Fats” Waller\, and othe
 rs in new arrangements from the director\, award-winning Declan Meagher (D
 isney Cruise Line).\nAward-winning playwright Natalie Kaye returns to come
 dy\, vaudeville and historical language since co-writing the Toronto Fring
 e 2025 hit #1 Clown Comedy With Victor & Priscilla\, a zany comedy with s
 old out nights and rave reviews including:\n“Hilarious” – THE TORON
 TO STAR\; “side-splittingly funny” – FRINGE REVIEW UK\; “bursting
