 24.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Step into Shakespeare’s world on this guided nature walk thr
 ough Toronto’s High Park\, where forest\, savannah\, and wetland habitat
 s become our living stage. We’ll explore how Shakespeare weaves the natu
 ral world into his language and stories\; where “the wind and the rain
 ” shape mood\, meaning\, and setting. As we walk\, we’ll reflect on th
 emes of transformation\, “the green world” of renewal\, and the shifti
 ng rhythms of seasons\, birdsong\, and wild landscapes.\nPrice: $10\nAges:
  16+ years\nMeeting Location: High Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodge
  Drive
