ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/12/original_image780a7681-c779-4497-97ca-dd688856d7
 82.jpg
DESCRIPTION:In an era of constant pings\, pop‑ups\, and pressure to stay
  connected\, our attention is pulled in every direction—yet most advice 
 focuses on screen‑time guilt rather than building real inner skills. Thi
 s interactive workshop offers a fresh approach grounded in the Stoic disci
 plines of Perception\, Action\, and Will. Through practical strategies\, y
 ou’ll explore how to notice digital pulls clearly\, respond with intenti
 on\, and stay aligned with your values amid everyday digital noise.\nRegis
 ter at https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a206482f56bd86e00b44522
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth Library
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-obstacle-is-the-phone-stoic-focus-in
 -a-distracted-digital-world-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:THROUGH Opening Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T210000
UID:blogto-236059@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/04/original_imageb8946c63-c4be-40ff-b2c9-d8b9ede417
 62.jpg
DESCRIPTION:New paintings by Mark Viola explore layered identity\, movemen
 t\, and perception through translucent\, process-driven works.\nNew Painti
 ngs by Mark Viola\nThrough explores translucence\, movement\, and the laye
 red nature of perception. Figures emerge and recede within surfaces that r
 eveal the process of their making\, inviting viewers to look beyond the im
 mediate image toward what lies beneath.\nAcross the exhibition\, the subje
 cts—ranging from cultural icons to creative genius—are approached not 
 as fixed images\, but as layered presences. Each carries a tension between
  public identity and private reality\, where visibility and vulnerability 
 coexist.\nThe works resist singular readings. Text fragments\, underlying 
 sketches\, and visible revisions surface through the painted image\, colla
 psing the division between foreground and background\, subject and process
 . What is typically concealed—mistakes\, adjustments\, earlier marks—r
 emains present\, forming a visual language that mirrors the complexity of 
 the individuals depicted.\nIn this way\, the act of painting becomes insep
 arable from the subject itself. The accumulation of layers echoes the psyc
 hological and emotional weight carried by each figure\, suggesting that id
 entity is not static\, but continuously constructed\, obscured\, and revea
 led over time.\nRather than offering resolution\, the works remain open—
 holding space for ambiguity\, motion\, and multiple readings. Through ulti
 mately asks not only what we see\, but how we see\, and what might be unco
 vered when we choose to look beyond the surface.
LOCATION:Twist Gallery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/through-opening-reception-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
