 b6.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Port Hope Salmon Festival\nis one of Ontario’s most exci
 ting fall traditions\, celebrating the incredible salmon migration along t
 he Ganaraska River in the heart of historic Port Hope. Held annually betwe
 en mid-August and mid-October\, the festival brings thousands of visitors 
 to watch massive Chinook and Coho salmon leap upstream at Corbett’s Dam 
 and the famous fish ladder\, creating an unforgettable natural spectacle. 
 Visitors can also enjoy local shops\, riverfront trails\, family activitie
 s\, food vendors\, live entertainment\, and the vibrant atmosphere through
 out downtown Port Hope.
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/port-hope-salmon-festival-toronto/
