 gto.com/events/2026/06/27/original_imageb541fa94-f058-427b-b326-85f9f613e9
 55.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Wavelength Summer Thing returns with double the stages!\nThis 
 annual celebration of live music returns to SummerSeries in Trillium Park.
  With a main stage and lake stage\, local talent will shine in genres rang
 ing from indie-folk to alternative hip-hop to Afro-Brazilian percussion.\n
 In addition to this all-Canadian line-up of performers\, the FREE event wi
 ll feature a mouth-watering selection of food and drink by the waterfront 
 park. Shop hand-made wares from independent vendors and participate in int
 eractive art installations for all ages.\nCelebrate summer how it’s mean
 t to be: together with some tunes by a toasty campfire and the lake!\nMain
  Stage\nShad (Toronto // rap powerhouse // 5x Polaris Short-Lister)\nAbsol
 ute Treat (Toronto // disco-rock pop // as heard on Heated Rivalry!)\nCJ W
 iley (Toronto // twangy guitar-rock anthems)\nTauro (Toronto // indie-soul
  piano // Cynthia Tauro + Brendan Canning of Broken Social Scene // Birthd
 ay Cake Records)\nJanette King (Montreal // alternative R&B)\nLake Stage\n
 Bells Larsen (Montreal // unconventional acoustic ballads)\nSister Ray (To
 ronto // expansive folk)\nDiar (دْيَار ) (Toronto // Arabic maqam wi
 th a Flamenco twist)\nMaracatu Mar Aberto (Toronto // Afro-Brazilian percu
