 gto.com/events/2026/04/28/original_image31104043-9f0f-4909-b099-db40852d7c
 97.jpg
DESCRIPTION:BINI is an eight-member Filipino girl group (Aiah\, Colet\, Ma
 loi\, Gwen\, Stacey\, Mikha\, Jhoanna\, and Sheena) redefining global pop.
  With more than 1 billion global streams from viral hits like “Cherry On
  Top” and a passionate global audience\, the octet has rapidly emerged a
 s one of Southeast Asia’s most influential musical forces. Crowned the P
 hilippines’ “Nation’s Girl Group\,” the octet has achieved a serie
 s of historic milestones\, including recognition as one of Spotify’s Bre
 akout Artists of 2024 and making history as the first Filipino group confi
 rmed on the lineup of Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival 2026. Fresh
  off major wins at the Awit Awards (GRAMMY’s equivalent in the Philippin
 es) and Brazil’s BreakTudo Awards\, BINI continues to champion the risin
 g global wave of Asian pop. Their previous album FLAMES followed a breakth
 rough year that included MTV Europe Music Awards Best Asia Act honors and 
 a standout feature in The Recording Academy’s GRAMMY list of “14 Pinoy
  Pop Acts You Should Know.” Named “Female Group of the Year” at the 
 Jupiter Music Awards 2025\, BINI stands at the forefront of Filipino pop
 ’s international ascent. With chart-topping releases\, sold-out arena sh
 ows including being the first Filipino act to sell out the Philippine Aren
 a (+50k)\, which is the world’s largest indoor arena\, a rapidly expandi
 ng global fan community known as Blooms\, the group has become a cultural 
 phenomenon bringing the vibrancy of Filipino pop to the world stage. As th
 ey celebrate the recent release of their new EP Signals\, BINI continues t
 o push the boundaries of pop\, proving they are not only the pride of the 
 Philippines but one of the most exciting rising forces in global music tod
 ay.
LOCATION:The Bowl at Sobeys Stadium
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/bini-signals-world-tour-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
