BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening with Steven Pinker
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T210000
UID:blogto-236703@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/18/original_imagea480aaeb-ac71-476e-bee8-a6e3354231
 d1.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Steven Pinker will appear live in Toronto for one night only a
 t the Queen Elizabeth Theatre on Tuesday 15 September 2026.\nOne of the wo
 rld’s most influential public thinkers\, Pinker is a Harvard psychologis
 t\, bestselling author and two-time Pulitzer Prize finalist whose work has
  shaped major conversations around language\, reason\, human nature\, viol
 ence and progress.\nPresented by Thinkable\, the evening will see Pinker e
 xplore the ideas behind landmark books including The Language Instinct\, T
 he Blank Slate\, The Better Angels of Our Nature and Enlightenment Now\, a
 longside themes from his latest work\, When Everyone Knows That Everyone K
 nows — a timely look at how shared knowledge shapes politics\, reputatio
 ns\, diplomacy\, social norms and collective behaviour.\nAt a moment of de
 ep polarisation\, collapsing public trust and contested ideas of progress\
 , Pinker’s Toronto appearance offers a compelling opportunity to examine
  how we think\, argue\, cooperate and make sense of the world.
LOCATION:Queen Elizabeth Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/an-evening-with-steven-pinker-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
