ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/23/original_image480f7dde-317b-4876-bb70-db28906a3c
 70.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Since 2010\, Next Music from Tokyo has brought some of the bes
 t indie/underground bands from Japan to perform in Toronto\, Montreal and 
 Vancouver.\nVolume 18 features:\n1. Haku. – all female indie-pop band wi
 th a cover song that went worldwide viral but still making noise with orig
 inal songs that slap even harder.  They were the biggest reason NMFT 17 so
 ld out so quickly so I had to bring them back again this year.   https://y
 outu.be/kDdTf2EinCs\n2. SYAYOS – an experimental pop band from Nagano wh
 ose music drifts seamlessly between folk\, soul\, and punk — think Kanek
 o Ayano meets Fugazi.   https://youtu.be/XuskwXYrBHs\n3. pudelhunds – an
  exceptionally talented trio performing intricately beautiful math rock wi
 th a bit of screamo    https://youtu.be/CPg7FH51Ots\n4. Yureruwayurei – 
 means ‘what quivers is a GHOST.’  Hailing from Okayama this 4pc crafts
  a melancholic blend of intense shoegaze and post-rock\, channeling a soun
 d reminiscent of NMFT favorites Kinoko Teikoku.    https://youtu.be/BevBa3
 -iWAQ\nThis is the first of two shows. All four bands play both nights.\nF
 or more info and tickets:  https://nextmusicfromtokyo.com
LOCATION:Horseshoe Tavern
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/next-music-from-tokyo-vol-18-1st-show-to
 ronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
