BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Interpol with support from DIIV
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261002T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261002T230000
UID:blogto-234437@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/30/original_image794fc90c-305f-49ca-873c-e0bec832df
 25.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Interpol’s seventh album The Other Side of Make-Believe find
 s the band exploring new emotional territory while staying true to their s
 ignature sound. Alongside the familiar dark undertones\, the record introd
 uces a sense of vulnerability\, grace\, and even hope\, with Paul Banks’
  more understated vocals and Daniel Kessler’s expansive guitar work push
 ing their music into fresh\, more introspective territory.\nWritten largel
 y in isolation during 2020 and completed in 2021 with producers Flood and 
 Alan Moulder\, the album reflects both the uncertainty of the times and a 
 deliberate shift toward resilience and emotional clarity. While themes of 
 distorted reality and modern disillusionment remain\, Interpol counterbala
 nces them with a focus on human strength and connection\, resulting in a r
 ecord that feels both reflective and quietly optimistic.
LOCATION:The Bowl at Sobeys Stadium
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/interpol-with-support-from-diiv-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
