BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BRAVO BEETHOVEN/ Homeland
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T213000
UID:blogto-235558@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/26/original_imaged4d9e3c2-15f7-470e-958e-3edb8f33aa
 fb.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Sinfonia Toronto's new season begins with a night that's equal
  parts celebration and discovery.\nOn October 3rd\, the orchestra welcomes
  internationally acclaimed pianist Sheng Cai for an evening anchored by tw
 o Beethoven favourites and the world premiere of Vahram Sargsyan's Ergir (
 Homeland)\, a deeply personal journey through ancestral melodies by a Jule
 s Léger Prize-winning composer. Joyful and nostalgic\, Homeland is rooted
  in ancestral memory\, and hearing it for the very first time will create 
 beautiful new memories.\nThe program opens with Beethoven's Piano Concerto
  No. 2\, bright and full of personality\, and closes as Maestro Nurhan Arm
 an leads the orchestra in Beethoven's "Harp" String Quartet in a lush orch
 estral version.\nTickets $20 (students) · $35.40 (seniors) · $45.20 (adu
 lts). Single tickets on sale June 1 at sinfoniatoronto.com.
LOCATION:Trinity-St. Paul's Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/bravo-beethoven-homeland-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
