BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tanglefoot Reunion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T230000
UID:blogto-235368@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/22/original_image285696ee-da7b-4763-885c-073759d3da
 a5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Songs\, The Stories\, The Spirit of Canada\nFor three deca
 des\, Tanglefoot carried the spirit of Canada across stages in North Ameri
 ca\, the United Kingdom\, and Europe with powerful harmonies\, quick wit\,
  rich storytelling\, and songs rooted in Canadian history. Now this legend
 ary Canadian folk ensemble returns for a special reunion concert\, bringin
 g their unmistakable energy\, warmth\, and humour back to the stage.\nThis
  new chapter reunites Canadian Folk Music Award winners Steve Ritchie\, Al
  Parrish\, Sandra Swannell Young\, and Rob Ritchie\, joined by Rob’s son
 \, singer and multi-instrumentalist Josh Ritchie\, stepping into the place
  once held by the late Terry Young. It is both a celebration of legacy and
  a fresh passing of the torch.\nAudiences can expect fan favourites\, hidd
 en gems\, stories\, laughter\, and the kind of heartfelt music that turns 
 a concert into a shared memory. For longtime fans\, this is a rare chance 
 to reconnect with a beloved part of Canadian folk music. For those discove
 ring Tanglefoot for the first time\, it is an invitation into songs that f
 eel timeless\, spirited\, and deeply Canadian.\nJoin us at Acoustic Harves
 t for an evening of friendship\, storytelling\, and music that reminds us 
 why live folk music still matters.
LOCATION:Acoustic Harvest
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/tanglefoot-reunion-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
